{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/queue/core_answers.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:46:34.562893Z","id":"14a47a285128cd657499d785b5825bfaaddf38abb8c20fc874cfe1232a8b038b","body":{"detail":"Mutations made in a scratch copy and reverted (none committed), each followed by bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:queue_update_properties_test: (1) disabling the moved-base guard in next.dart (`if (publish.base < known)`, the one that keeps a finish planned on a refused base from publishing again): PASSED. Every generated finish plans on input.base (core_answers.dart:503-516), so the model never plans on a stale base and _onePublishPerBase's last check never fires. (2) removing both `if (running >= QueueModel.maxRunning) return true;` guards of Keep going and Retry (next.dart:165, :177): PASSED; no unit test covers them either (update_test.dart has only 'queued, three running → nothing'). (3) removing the stale-turn drop in TurnDone (update.dart, `job.step != …`): PASSED, as did update_test; the drop looks unreachable with one owner. For contrast, removing the queued gate (`running < QueueModel.maxRunning` at next.dart:127) fails at run 537. The generator also never cancels a job from the core's side (artifact_going_tx's cancel with artifact_deleted) or purges its row (JobRead with null, the _forget path), and it has no coverage key for either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":492},"end":{"line":519},"content_hash":"adfd0e3081ee42c35831ed8627a3a4c8bd76ef684cdc5e2fa8ee9e190357662e"},"suggested_fix":"Let a finish plan on job.input.base or a base below input.base now and then; grant Keep going and Retry while three run (and add coverage keys 'keep going held at the limit', 'retry held at the limit', 'read: no row', 'cancelled by the core'); add a FakeJobsCore.deleteArtifact that cancels with artifact_deleted and later drops the row; add update_test cases for Keep going and Retry held at three running.","summary":"The property generator never reaches three of the guards it is meant to check: removing each still passes the property test","tags":["review","queue","task-24","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/queue/core_answers.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:35:35.115267Z","id":"d47b228ac4c19a879dee954e8b36e3491c19ba696aaaf9902f19dbc165c7af46","body":{"detail":"Evidence (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:queue_update_properties_test, seed 42, 2,000 runs, 41,157 messages, each scratch mutation reverted): removing the moved-base guard (next.dart, finish when publish.base < job.base) fails at run 14 message 11 'publish:1 is on a base the core refused as moved'; removing both run-limit guards of Keep going and Retry fails at run 228 message 18 's3 started while {s0, s1, s2} run'; removing the stale-turn drop (update.dart TurnDone) fails at run 89 message 22 'turn:2 of m3 is committed'. Unmutated it passes, reaching keep going held at the limit 6, retry held 7, stale turn dropped 21, read: no row 25, cancelled by the core 687, finish on a stale base 705. Seed 20261020 passed too, run once. Unit tests in update_test.dart: Keep going and Retry held at three running and granted when one ends; 'another writer commits the turn: the stale one commits nothing'.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:54362aacc","summary":"Fixed in 54362aacc: the generator plans finishes on older bases, holds Keep going and Retry at the limit, has another writer commit a running job's turn, cancels jobs with artifact_deleted, purges rows, and seeds a third of the runs with a killed worker's jobs; new coverage keys and a start-under-the-limit invariant","supersedes":"14a47a285128cd657499d785b5825bfaaddf38abb8c20fc874cfe1232a8b038b","tags":["reason:fixed","queue","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/queue/codec_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:39:24.028076Z","id":"eb184f5620c2c61de5924d23e8fec9b0f39f69f4d4273ef76ad08a87059a8b97","body":{"detail":"Committed, Refused, JobRead, TurnDone, TurnFailed, ToolDone, Rendered, RenderLost, the ClaimAnswer types, OwnerChanged, JobsLoaded, CanRender, ClaudeReachable, Tick and Woke (lib/queue/msg.dart) and the Refusal types NotRenderedClean, JobMoved, NotOwner and Invalid compare by identity. The test also checks that the re-encoded value equals the first encoding, which does not catch a field the encoder never writes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":428},"end":{"line":483},"content_hash":"66132e9ff3e64406d0135f9ef66f2ec7ed4250c11d8c1791f600c6eeeb3cbbf2"},"suggested_fix":"Give those classes value equality in lib/queue/msg.dart, then compare decoded messages with == and delete msgFields.","summary":"Most Msg types have no ==, so the codec's round-trip test compares them through msgFields: a field added to such a message must be added here too, or a codec that drops it still passes","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/queue/codec_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:31:33.042034Z","id":"7c4c2cfa30792d56be5e06d98b3c1787a8c674aa13228a13980f033f8a3adf39","body":{"detail":"Committed, Refused, JobRead, TurnDone, TurnFailed, ToolDone, Rendered, RenderLost, the ClaimAnswer types, OwnerChanged, JobsLoaded, CanRender, ClaudeReachable, Tick and Woke (lib/queue/msg.dart) and the Refusal types NotRenderedClean, JobMoved, NotOwner and Invalid compare by identity. The test also checks that the re-encoded value equals the first encoding, which does not catch a field the encoder never writes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":428},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"a19f3dc6b039e621c309697c77504645d500f0f5c2f3140cff1cafa681809d9a"},"suggested_fix":"Give those classes value equality in lib/queue/msg.dart, then compare decoded messages with == and delete msgFields.","summary":"Most Msg types have no ==, so the codec's round-trip test compares them through msgFields: a field added to such a message must be added here too, or a codec that drops it still passes","supersedes":"eb184f5620c2c61de5924d23e8fec9b0f39f69f4d4273ef76ad08a87059a8b97","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
